@cabinet_success
title: The democratic cabinet takes office
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
Q.formation_complete = 1;
Q.caretaker_government = 0;
Q.government_has_confidence = 1;
Q.prime_minister = Q.democratic_candidate;
Q.government_name = Q.democratic_candidate + " democratic coalition";
if (Q.democratic_candidate == "Donald Tusk") {
    Q.government_party = "ko";
    Q.government_owner = "KO-led democratic coalition";
} else if (Q.democratic_candidate == "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz") {
    Q.government_party = "psl";
    Q.government_owner = "PSL-led democratic coalition";
} else if (Q.democratic_candidate == "Agnieszka Dziemianowicz-Bąk") {
    Q.government_party = Q.left_cabinet_committed
        ? "lewica" : "independent";
    Q.government_owner = Q.left_cabinet_committed
        ? "Lewica-led democratic coalition"
        : "Independent parliamentary cabinet";
} else {
    Q.government_party = "other";
    Q.government_owner = Q.democratic_candidate + " parliamentary cabinet";
}
Q.left_in_government = Q.left_cabinet_committed ? 1 : 0;
const cabinetPartyLabels = [];
if (Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet) cabinetPartyLabels.push("KO");
if (Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet) cabinetPartyLabels.push("Poland 2050");
if (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet) cabinetPartyLabels.push("PSL");
if (Q.left_in_government) cabinetPartyLabels.push("Lewica");
Q.coalition_status = cabinetPartyLabels.join(" · ") + " cabinet";
Q.coalition_seats = Math.min(
    Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460,
    (Q.ministry_ko_in_cabinet
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0)
        : 0) +
    (Q.ministry_p2050_in_cabinet
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0)
        : 0) +
    (Q.ministry_psl_in_cabinet
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0)
        : 0) +
    (Q.left_in_government
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats) || 0)
        : 0)
);
const nonLeftCabinetSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.coalition_seats -
        (Q.left_in_government
            ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.ministry_left_cabinet_seats) || 0)
            : 0)
);
Q.government_support_seats = Math.max(
    nonLeftCabinetSeats,
    Math.max(
        0,
        (Number(Q.democratic_votes) || 0) -
            (Number(Q.candidate_left_votes) || 0)
    )
);
Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = Q.government_party;
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.position = "Coalition government";
    Q.budget = 6;
    Q.budget_authority = "Governing coalition — negotiated fiscal capacity";
    Q.ending_name = "The Left enters government";
    if (Q.formation_continuous) {
        Q.formation_outcome_score = 48;
        Q.ending_score =
            (Number.isFinite(Number(Q.ending_score))
                ? Number(Q.ending_score)
                : 0) + 8;
    } else {
        Q.ending_score = 48;
    }
} else {
    Q.position = "Confidence-and-supply opposition";
    Q.budget = 0;
    Q.budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority";
    Q.ending_name = "Support without office";
    if (Q.formation_continuous) {
        Q.formation_outcome_score = 32;
        Q.ending_score =
            (Number.isFinite(Number(Q.ending_score))
                ? Number(Q.ending_score)
                : 0) + 3;
    } else {
        Q.ending_score = 32;
    }
}
!}

= Office is a constitutional fact

**[+ prime_minister +]** now leads the cabinet. The Left's constitutional
position follows the agreement actually made, not the colour of the deputies
who voted yes.

[? if left_in_government = 1: Lewica has ministers and collective
responsibility. The government budget and coalition-management game is now
available. ?]

[? if left_in_government = 0: Lewica supplied confidence without taking
ministries. It can bargain over bills, but it does not control the state budget
and receives no governing-spend actions. ?]

