@article160_survives
title: A majority, or merely more yes than no
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: ending_name = "The cabinet survives confidence"; ending_score += 12

The cabinet remains in office because **[+ confidence_yes +] yes** exceeded
**[+ confidence_no +] no** with quorum. That is not an absolute majority and
does not guarantee the next ordinary bill; every vote must reproduce the
necessary support or abstention.

- @constructive_motion: Let the opposition try to name a replacement
- @resolution_exit: Record the confidence result

@article160_falls
title: The prime minister resigns
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: left_in_government = 0; caretaker_government = 1; position = "Caretaker cabinet and new formation talks"; budget = 0; budget_authority = "Caretaker — no new governing-spend actions"; coalition_status = "Cabinet lost confidence"; coalition_seats = 0; ending_name = "Confidence lost"; ending_score -= 12

The loss is not a constructive vote: it removes confidence without installing a
named successor. A new formation sequence begins. Lewica's ministers remain
caretakers for continuity, but the player no longer receives government budget
actions.

- @formation_exit: Record the fall

@constructive_motion
title: A constructive vote of no confidence
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and formation_in_progress = 0

= Article 158 — 46 signatures, one named successor

Opponents cannot merely vote the cabinet out. At least 46 deputies must sign a
motion naming a replacement prime minister; the Sejm waits seven days; at least
231 deputies must then vote yes. If it fails, another motion normally waits
three months unless at least 115 deputies sign.

PiS supplies the signatures. The struggle is over which candidate can turn
separate party crises into 231 votes.

- @constructive_defend
- @constructive_psl_right
- @constructive_trzaskowski
- @constructive_kosiniak

@constructive_defend
title: Defend the cabinet against Beata Szydło
subtitle: Test the actual right-wing seat total; no party is granted phantom votes.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
const rightSeats =
    Math.max(0, Q.pis_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.konf_seats) +
    Math.max(0, Q.rozwoj_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.korona_seats);
const governmentSeats = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        Q.sejm_total - rightSeats,
        Number.isFinite(Number(Q.coalition_seats))
            ? Math.round(Number(Q.coalition_seats))
            : Q.coalition_democratic_seats
    )
);
Q.constructive_candidate = "Beata Szydło";
Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.min(
    rightSeats,
    Math.max(46, Math.min(115, rightSeats))
);
Q.constructive_yes = rightSeats;
Q.constructive_no = governmentSeats;
Q.constructive_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.sejm_total - Q.constructive_yes - Q.constructive_no
);
Q.constructive_democratic = 0;
Q.news_headline = rightSeats >= Q.sejm_statutory_majority
    ? "The right has assembled a constructive majority"
    : "The right cannot turn its challenge into 231 votes";
!}
go-to: constructive_roll

@constructive_psl_right
title: Let PSL cross to a Szydło social-conservative cabinet
subtitle: Deliverable PSL votes follow current relations and caucus dissent.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: {!
const rightSeats =
    Math.max(0, Q.pis_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.konf_seats) +
    Math.max(0, Q.rozwoj_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.korona_seats);
const pslDiscipline = Math.max(
    0,
    Math.min(
        Math.max(0, Q.psl_seats),
        Math.round(
            Math.max(0, Q.psl_seats) *
            Math.max(
                0.25,
                Math.min(
                    1,
                    (105 - Math.max(0, Q.psl_relation)) / 75 +
                    Math.max(0, Q.psl_coalition_dissent) / 250
                )
            )
        )
    )
);
Q.constructive_candidate = "Beata Szydło";
Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.min(
    rightSeats,
    Math.max(46, Math.min(115, rightSeats))
);
Q.constructive_yes = rightSeats + pslDiscipline;
Q.constructive_no = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.ko_seats + Q.p2050_seats + Q.centrum_seats +
    Q.left_committed_seats
);
Q.constructive_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.sejm_total - Q.constructive_yes - Q.constructive_no
);
Q.constructive_democratic = 0;
Q.psl_relation -= 25;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent = 100;
Q.far_right_agenda += 8;
Q.news_headline = pslDiscipline + " PSL deputies cross to Szydło";
!}
go-to: constructive_roll

@constructive_trzaskowski
title: Replace [+ prime_minister +] with Rafał Trzaskowski inside the democratic majority
subtitle: A KO rupture tests the coalition's current seats and PSL discipline.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and president_name != "Rafał Trzaskowski" and prime_minister != "Rafał Trzaskowski"
on-arrival: {!
const rightSeats =
    Math.max(0, Q.pis_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.konf_seats) +
    Math.max(0, Q.rozwoj_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.korona_seats);
const pslLoss = Math.min(
    Math.max(0, Q.psl_seats),
    Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(
            (45 - Math.max(0, Q.psl_relation)) / 5 +
            Math.max(0, Q.psl_coalition_dissent - 45) / 10
        )
    )
);
Q.constructive_candidate = "Rafał Trzaskowski";
Q.constructive_yes = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.coalition_democratic_seats - pslLoss
);
Q.constructive_no = rightSeats;
Q.constructive_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.sejm_total - Q.constructive_yes - Q.constructive_no
);
Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.min(
    115,
    Math.max(46, Q.constructive_yes)
);
Q.constructive_democratic = 1;
Q.ko_coalition_dissent += 18;
Q.progressives_dissent -= 5;
Q.news_headline =
    "KO tests a constructive replacement with " +
    Q.constructive_yes + " declared votes";
!}
go-to: constructive_roll

@constructive_kosiniak
title: Reset the coalition around Kosiniak-Kamysz
subtitle: A centrist compromise begins with the currently committed democratic clubs.
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and president_name != "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz" and prime_minister != "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz"
on-arrival: {!
const rightSeats =
    Math.max(0, Q.pis_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.konf_seats) +
    Math.max(0, Q.rozwoj_seats) + Math.max(0, Q.korona_seats);
Q.constructive_candidate = "Władysław Kosiniak-Kamysz";
Q.constructive_yes = Math.max(0, Q.coalition_democratic_seats);
Q.constructive_no = rightSeats;
Q.constructive_abstain = Math.max(
    0,
    Q.sejm_total - Q.constructive_yes - Q.constructive_no
);
Q.constructive_sponsors = Math.min(
    115,
    Math.max(46, Q.constructive_yes)
);
Q.constructive_democratic = 1;
Q.psl_relation += 10;
Q.psl_coalition_dissent -= 15;
Q.progressive_credibility -= 5;
Q.feminist_trust -= 5;
Q.news_headline = "The coalition tests a centrist constructive replacement";
!}
go-to: constructive_roll

@constructive_roll
title: The named replacement
new-page: true
view-if: left_in_government = 1 and government_has_confidence = 1 and caretaker_government = 0 and formation_in_progress = 0
on-arrival: {!
Q.confidence_stage = 6;
Q.confidence_mode =
    "Article 158 constructive no confidence — statutory majority";
Q.confidence_candidate = Q.constructive_candidate;
Q.confidence_yes = Q.constructive_yes;
Q.confidence_no = Q.constructive_no;
Q.confidence_abstain = Q.constructive_abstain;
Q.confidence_present =
    Q.confidence_yes + Q.confidence_no + Q.confidence_abstain;
Q.confidence_threshold = 231;
Q.constructive_passed =
    Q.constructive_sponsors >= 46 &&
    Q.confidence_yes >= Q.sejm_statutory_majority ? 1 : 0;
if (Q.constructive_passed) {
    Q.prime_minister = Q.constructive_candidate;
    Q.government_name = Q.constructive_candidate + " constructive cabinet";
    Q.government_has_confidence = 1;
    Q.caretaker_government = 0;
    Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
    Q.formation_complete = 1;
    Q.coalition_broken = 0;
    Q.constructive_vonc_cooldown = 0;
    if (Q.constructive_democratic) {
        const constructiveCandidateKey =
            String(Q.constructive_candidate || "").toLowerCase();
        if (constructiveCandidateKey.includes("kosiniak")) {
            Q.government_party = "psl";
            Q.government_owner = "PSL-led coalition";
        } else {
            Q.government_party = "ko";
            Q.government_owner = "KO-led democratic coalition";
        }
        Q.left_in_government = 1;
        Q.left_cabinet_committed = 1;
        Q.position = "Coalition government";
        Q.coalition_status = "Reconstituted democratic coalition";
        Q.ending_name = "A constructive democratic replacement";
        Q.ending_score += 8;
    } else {
        Q.government_party = "pis";
        Q.government_owner = "PiS and its governing partners";
        Q.left_in_government = 0;
        Q.left_cabinet_committed = 0;
        Q.left_cabinet_model = "Opposition";
        Q.ministries_finalized = 1;
        Q.ministry_allocation_mode = "settled";
        Q.position = "Parliamentary opposition";
        Q.coalition_status = "PiS · Konfederacja · PSL constructive majority";
        Q.budget = 0;
        Q.budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority";
        const constructiveRightCabinet = {
            labor: ["PiS", "Dorota Bojemska"],
            equality: ["PiS", "Anna Schmidt"],
            housing: ["PiS", "Piotr Uściński"],
            health: ["PiS", "Ewa Krajewska"],
            digital: ["PiS", "Janusz Cieszyński"],
            science: ["PiS", "Krzysztof Szczucki"],
            interior: ["PiS", "Paweł Szefernaker"],
            finance: ["PiS", "Andrzej Kosztowniak"],
            economy: ["PiS", "Marlena Maląg"],
            justice: ["PiS", "Marcin Warchoł"],
            foreign: ["PiS", "Szymon Szynkowski vel Sęk"],
            agriculture: ["PiS", "Anna Gembicka"],
            defence: ["PiS", "Mariusz Błaszczak"]
        };
        for (
            const portfolio of Object.keys(
                constructiveRightCabinet
            )
        ) {
            Q[portfolio + "_minister_party"] =
                constructiveRightCabinet[portfolio][0];
            Q[portfolio + "_minister"] =
                constructiveRightCabinet[portfolio][1];
        }
        Q.family_minister_party = Q.labor_minister_party;
        Q.family_minister = Q.labor_minister;
        Q.ministry_count = 0;
        Q.cabinet_roster_government_party = "pis";
        Q.ending_name = "The coalition crosses right";
        Q.ending_score -= 18;
    }
    Q.coalition_seats = Q.government_party == "pis"
        ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.pis_seats) || 0)
        : Math.min(
            Number(Q.sejm_total) || 460,
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.ko_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.p2050_seats) || 0) +
            Math.max(0, Number(Q.psl_seats) || 0) +
            (Q.left_in_government
                ? Math.max(0, Number(Q.left_seats) || 0)
                : 0)
        );
    const constructiveYes = Math.max(
        0,
        Math.round(Number(Q.constructive_yes) || 0)
    );
    const constructiveLeftVotes = Q.constructive_democratic
        ? Math.min(
            constructiveYes,
            Math.max(0, Math.round(Number(Q.left_committed_seats) || 0))
        )
        : 0;
    Q.government_support_seats =
        constructiveYes - constructiveLeftVotes;
    Q.news_headline =
        Q.constructive_candidate + " replaces the prime minister immediately";
} else {
    Q.constructive_vonc_cooldown = 3;
    Q.ending_name = "The constructive motion fails";
    Q.ending_score += 6;
    Q.news_headline =
        "The constructive motion fails and enters a three-month cooldown";
}
!}

= Constructive roll call

<div class="ledger-section ledger-section-first"><div class="ledger-title">Roll
call</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Named successor</span><b>[+ confidence_candidate +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Sponsors</span><b>[+ constructive_sponsors +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Yes</span><b>[+ confidence_yes +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>No</span><b>[+ confidence_no +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Abstain</span><b>[+ confidence_abstain +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Required</span><b>231</b></div></div>

[? if constructive_passed: The named candidate becomes prime minister. No
intervening vacuum and no separate destructive removal vote exist. ?]

[? if not constructive_passed: The sitting cabinet remains. The ordinary
three-month cooldown is now recorded. ?]

- @resolution_exit: Record the result

@formation_exit
title: Return from the formation crisis
go-to: campaign_return if formation_continuous = 1; opposition_assessment if formation_continuous = 0

@resolution_exit
title: Return from the government crisis
go-to: campaign_return if formation_continuous = 1; assessment if formation_continuous = 0

@campaign_return
title: Return to the monthly campaign
new-page: true
view-if: formation_continuous = 1
on-arrival: {!
const returnYear = 2023;
const returnMonth = 12;
const currentYear = Number(Q.year) || returnYear;
const currentMonth = Number(Q.month) || returnMonth;
const skippedMonths = Math.max(
    0,
    (returnYear - currentYear) * 12 + returnMonth - currentMonth
);
Q.time = Math.max(0, Number(Q.time) || 0) + skippedMonths;
Q.formation_in_progress = 0;
Q.formation_return_ready = 1;
Q.formation_requested = 0;
Q.formation_complete = 1;
Q.election_2023_certified = 1;
Q.post_formation_return_pending = 0;
Q.prototype_complete = 0;
Q.year = returnYear;
Q.month = returnMonth;
Q.month_name = "December";
Q.date_label = "December 2023";
if (!Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.budget = 0;
    Q.budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority";
}
Q.news_headline =
    Q.prime_minister + " leaves the formation crisis with " +
    Q.coalition_seats + " declared supporting seats";
!}
go-to: poland_event_queue

@opposition_assessment
title: Opposition has leverage, not a treasury
new-page: true
on-arrival: left_in_government = 0; budget = 0; budget_authority = "Opposition — no state spending authority"; annual_budget_done = 0

= The Left outside the cabinet

Lewica may still be pivotal on statutes, presidential veto overrides,
investigatory commissions and future confidence motions. It does not possess
government fiscal capacity. The governing budget path is therefore closed
rather than reskinned as opposition spending.

- @assessment: Close the formation chapter

@assessment
title: Transfer-of-power assessment
new-page: true
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.left_in_government) {
    Q.ending_score += Math.round(Q.party_unity / 10);
    Q.ending_score += Math.round(Q.public_trust / 10);
    if (Q.annual_budget_passed) Q.ending_score += 10;
} else {
    Q.ending_score += Math.round(Q.party_unity / 12);
}
Q.prototype_complete = 1;
!}

= [+ ending_name +]

<div class="ledger-section ledger-section-first"><div class="ledger-title">Final
position</div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Prime minister</span><b>[+ prime_minister +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Cabinet</span><b>[+ government_name +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Lewica</span><b>[+ position +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Left unity</span><b>[+ party_unity +]/100</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Coalition status</span><b>[+ coalition_status +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Last confidence procedure</span><b>[+ confidence_mode +]</b></div>
<div class="ledger-row"><span>Score</span><b>[+ ending_score +]</b></div></div>

[? if left_in_government = 1: Lewica retains cabinet responsibility. It has
won access to policy at the price of being answerable for every compromise,
every PSL ultimatum and the next annual budget. ?]

[? if left_in_government = 0: Lewica ends outside the cabinet. Its resources
remain party resources; no government budget currency is displayed or
actionable. ?]

This vertical slice treats parliamentary arithmetic as politics rather than a
single “coalition stability” bar: nominations, cabinet confidence, budgets,
prime-ministerial confidence and constructive replacement each obey their own
rule.

- @replay: Replay the 2023 formation chapter
- @return_title: Return to the title

@replay
go-to: setup

@return_title
on-arrival: started = 0; formation_requested = 0
go-to: root
